WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.160
One thing just about everyone in the&nbsp;
"Star Wars" universe can agree on is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.720
that you don't want to wind up on the&nbsp;
business end of a lightsaber. But as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.800
deadly as these weapons seem, some have lived&nbsp;
to tell the tale of being attacked with one.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.680
When The Phantom Menace premiered in 1999, the&nbsp;
only thing that just about every Star Wars fan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.080
could agree on was that Darth Maul was one&nbsp;
of the best parts of the movie. His signature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.640
look frightened younger audiences, and his&nbsp;
double-bladed lightsaber changed the game forever.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.840
Though he doesn't say a whole lot,&nbsp;
Maul's commanding presence makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.440
the character work. That final "Duel&nbsp;
of the Fates" sequence at the climax&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.600
of the film proved to all that this Sith&nbsp;
apprentice was a force to be reckoned with.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.680
After killing Jedi Master Qui-Gon Jinn in brutal&nbsp;
combat, Maul nearly dispatches a young Obi-Wan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:49.711
Kenobi as well. Pinning our hero down, Maul taunts&nbsp;
Kenobi, kicking his lightsaber into the abyss.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.711 --> 00:00:55.880
However, Obi-Wan surprises Maul and cuts the Sith&nbsp;
literally in two, sending him down into the void.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.560
For years, it seemed as if Maul was&nbsp;
dead, though some Star Wars Legends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:03.840
stories claimed he survived. This led to&nbsp;
his eventual resurrection in Star Wars:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.320
The Clone Wars, where it was revealed&nbsp;
that Maul, now a cyborg, remained alive.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.240
Voiced by Sam Witwer, Maul lived on with an&nbsp;
intense hatred for Kenobi and confronted his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:17.320
nemesis on numerous occasions. Maul&nbsp;
also led the Crimson Dawn criminal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:22.320
syndicate depicted in Solo, but was soon&nbsp;
side-tracked by his revenge. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:28.920
Maul was officially killed by Kenobi in Star&nbsp;
Wars Rebels, having finally found peace.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.240
Few have gone through as much pain and&nbsp;
suffering in the Star Wars universe as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.880
Anakin Skywalker. Be it emotional&nbsp;
turmoil or physical deterioration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.720
Anakin has undergone enough hardship&nbsp;
to last two lifetimes. For this reason,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:46.360
it's somewhat fitting that he lived out two lives:&nbsp;
one as a Jedi Knight and the other as a Sith Lord.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:51.200
In Attack of the Clones, Anakin and Obi-Wan&nbsp;
engage the Sith Lord Count Dooku in battle, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.640
though the young padawan has undergone rigorous&nbsp;
training, he was unprepared for this match.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:00.480
As master and apprentice tackled the Sith,&nbsp;
Dooku gained the upper hand and took Anakin's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:05.080
arm off below the elbow. Sending the padawan&nbsp;
backward, Dooku would've finished the job had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:09.800
Master Yoda not arrived in time to fend off&nbsp;
the Sith Lord. Gaining a cybernetic limb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:13.280
Anakin recovers from his wound,&nbsp;
using his newfound robotic parts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.600
to his advantage during the Clone Wars. He&nbsp;
even returns the favor to Dooku two fold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.840
by removing both of the Sith Lord’s hands&nbsp;
before decapitating him in Revenge of the Sith.

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:27.600
"It is only natural. He cut off&nbsp;
your arm, you wanted revenge."

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.720
Unfortunately for the young Jedi, later in&nbsp;
the film Anakin takes on his former master&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:36.320
on the volcanic planet Mustafar. After a&nbsp;
long duel, Kenobi gains the high ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:41.040
removing both of Anakin's legs and his&nbsp;
remaining arm in the process. By the film's end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:46.080
Anakin is given more cybernetic replacements,&nbsp;
having now become the Lord Vader we all know.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.680
Technically, Vader also lost yet another&nbsp;
arm to his son Luke in Return of the Jedi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:54.240
though he didn't live for very long afterward.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.360
In The Empire Strikes Back, Luke arrives at&nbsp;
Cloud City to save his friends from Vader's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:03.480
force-choking grasp, only to learn that the entire&nbsp;
thing is a set-up. Cornered by the Sith Lord,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:07.560
Luke strikes back, and even lands&nbsp;
a blow on Vader's armor. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:13.160
it isn't enough, and soon Vader overpowers&nbsp;
him, taking his right hand in the process.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:18.560
Just as Anakin lost his arm to a Sith Lord in his&nbsp;
youth, Luke loses his hand to Darth Vader. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:23.901
here that Vader attempts to sway Luke to the dark&nbsp;
side, and reveals the young Jedis' true parentage.

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:27.960
"No, I am your father."

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:32.200
Thankfully, Luke doesn't succumb to the same&nbsp;
temptations from either his father or the Emperor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:37.174
that Anakin once did. Instead he resists,&nbsp;
finding refuge in his love for his friends.

00:03:37.174 --> 00:03:41.800
However, like his father, Luke receives a&nbsp;
cybernetic replacement as a result. His wound,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:46.840
paired with the capture of his friend Han Solo,&nbsp;
serves as a powerful motivator, and Luke acquires&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:51.840
all the skills necessary to become a full-fledged&nbsp;
Jedi Knight by the events of Return of the Jedi.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:57.560
Luke soon establishes a new Jedi order, and by the&nbsp;
sequel trilogy, he remains unscarred any further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:02.880
at least physically, thus removing&nbsp;
his destiny from that of his father.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:07.720
It may be surprising to learn that Obi-Wan Kenobi&nbsp;
has suffered some pretty deadly lightsaber wounds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:11.800
but fans of the Star Wars prequel trilogy&nbsp;
will likely remember these scars well.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:16.160
During the same battle with Count Dooku that&nbsp;
resulted in Anakin's arm being chopped off,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:19.352
Obi-Wan too was singed by&nbsp;
the red blade of the Sith&nbsp;&nbsp; Lord. 

00:04:19.401 --> 00:04:24.720
Early in the battle, Skywalker is incapacitated&nbsp;
with Force lightning forcing Kenobi to face off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:29.720
against the Sith Lord alone. Given that this is&nbsp;
the second Sith he's faced, his training proves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:35.240
true and the Jedi Knight fends off Dooku for&nbsp;
quite awhile. Unfortunately for Kenobi, Dooku does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:40.640
eventually prevail and cuts him deep in the arm&nbsp;
and the leg. It is after Obi-Wan is injured that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:46.080
Anakin faces the count again before losing his&nbsp;
arm. Yoda then must rescue the two younger Jedi.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:50.560
Of course, this isn't the only lightsaber wound&nbsp;
that Obi-Wan endures. In the original Star Wars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:56.520
film, A New Hope, old Ben Kenobi faces off against&nbsp;
Darth Vader, sacrificing himself to give Luke and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:01.160
his friends the chance to escape. Though it's&nbsp;
debatable if the blade actually touches old Ben&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:07.520
or if he just disintegrates into the force, he&nbsp;
returns as a spirit in the sequel nonetheless.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.840
One of the primary antagonists&nbsp;
from the animated Star Wars Rebels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:15.200
the Grand Inquisitor is at the top of the food&nbsp;
chain among the Force-sensitive Jedi assassins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:20.080
known as the Empire's Inquisitorius. Having&nbsp;
been once trained as a Jedi Temple Guard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.760
the Grand Inquisitor fell to the Dark&nbsp;
Side and joined the Galactic Empire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.200
after the end of the Clone Wars, committing&nbsp;
himself fully to the service of the Emperor.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:31.880
Allied with Darth Vader, the Grand&nbsp;
Inquisitor helped exterminate Jedi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:36.720
all over — at least until the events of the&nbsp;
Obi-Wan Kenobi series. In the Disney+ show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.920
the Grand Inquisitor is seemingly killed&nbsp;
after he's betrayed by Reva, also known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:45.800
as the Third Sister, who shoves her lightsaber&nbsp;
through him in order to surpass him in power.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:49.880
As a result, Reva is given his title&nbsp;
and he's seemingly forgotten. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:54.000
it's later revealed that he survived due&nbsp;
to his thirst for vengeance. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.960
the Grand Inquisitor is given back his&nbsp;
title, serving under Darth Vader once more.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:04.160
"Revenge does wonders for the&nbsp;
will to live, don't you think?"

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:08.800
Since Rebels takes place after the events of&nbsp;
Obi-Wan Kenobi, the Grand Inquisitor eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:13.880
allows himself to die in a battle with Ezra&nbsp;
Bridger and Kanan Jarrus. Later on, it's revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:21.120
that his spirit was redeemed, and he becomes known&nbsp;
as The Sentinel, a spiritual ally to the Jedi.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:25.840
Speaking of Inquisitors, Reva too survived&nbsp;
a lightsaber wound. Even more impressively,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:30.840
she survived mortal combat with Darth&nbsp;
Vader himself, twice. In Obi-Wan Kenobi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:36.160
we learn that Reva was a Youngling at the Jedi&nbsp;
Temple on Coruscant when Order 66 was given,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:40.080
and she faced down against Anakin&nbsp;
Skywalker as he slaughtered her peers.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.000
Somehow, she survived being stabbed by the former&nbsp;
Jedi Knight and grew to hate him. Deducing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:49.400
Skywalker and Vader were one and the same,&nbsp;
she planned to assassinate him for revenge.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:53.920
As Reva and Vader battle, we see the full&nbsp;
scope of the Sith Lord's power. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:58.880
the Dark Lord stabs her again, seemingly&nbsp;
killing her, now for the second time. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:02.920
she doesn't die. Somehow, Reva's rage and&nbsp;
connection to the Dark Side of the Force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:07.600
keep her from death, and she soon flees&nbsp;
to Tatooine to kill Vader's only son.

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:11.320
Thankfully, she decides against slaughtering&nbsp;
a young boy in the same way that Vader once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:15.240
attempted to kill her, leaving her&nbsp;
story open to be revisited again.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:19.640
Of all the characters on this list, Reva's&nbsp;
survival is arguably the most outlandish.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:23.720
It's one thing to survive a lightsaber&nbsp;
wound as an adult, but as a young child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:26.960
it seems just a little far-fetched.&nbsp;
Perhaps the Force — or the Obi-Wan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:32.600
Kenobi showrunners — have big plans for&nbsp;
her in coming Star Wars installments.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:36.320
Originally a main character from the&nbsp;
animated Star Wars Rebels, Sabine Wren&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:40.880
is a Mandalorian-turned-Jedi apprentice who&nbsp;
goes on a quest to find her long-lost friend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:45.800
Ezra Bridger in the Disney+ series "Ahsoka."&nbsp;
Having been trained in the Jedi arts by Ahsoka&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:50.800
Tano in the years between Rebels and the Ahsoka&nbsp;
series, Sabine and her former master parted ways&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:56.389
some time ago. However, when Ahsoka needs her help&nbsp;
finding Ezra, Sabine jumps back into the fight.

00:07:56.389 --> 00:08:00.520
Unfortunately for our heroes, they're not the&nbsp;
only ones in need of the map that will help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:04.760
them find Ezra. It turns out the device&nbsp;
will also help some Empire-sympathizers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:08.960
find Grand Admiral Thrawn. To get it&nbsp;
back, Dark Jedi apprentice Shin Hati&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.880
surprises Sabine, stealing the map&nbsp;
and engaging in a lightsaber duel.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:16.800
During the battle, Shin stabs Sabine through&nbsp;
the gut, leaving her for dead. Though it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.920
might have been easy to assume the worst, the&nbsp;
opening of the very next episode reveals that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.920 --> 00:08:25.040
somehow, Sabine survived, with&nbsp;
only a small scar to show for it.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:29.680
Strangely, unlike others who have survived such&nbsp;
intense lightsaber wounds, Sabine seems to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:33.920
needed no cybernetic implants. Whether&nbsp;
that's true or not remains to be seen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:37.840
but given the intensity of the injury, it&nbsp;
seems like there should've been some major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:44.200
repercussions. After all, it's the same wound&nbsp;
that killed Qui-Gon Jinn in The Phantom Menace.

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:48.840
The only non-Force user on this list, General&nbsp;
Grievous is a cyborg and a major figure in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:53.480
Confederacy of Independent Systems. A serious&nbsp;
thorn in our heroes' sides throughout the Clone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.360
Wars, Grievous actually first appeared&nbsp;
in the original animated Star Wars:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:01.280
Clone Wars series ahead of the release&nbsp;
of Revenge of the Sith. By Episode III,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:06.240
General Grievous was known as a notorious Jedi&nbsp;
killer who would collect their blades as trophies.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:11.640
"Your lightsabers will make a&nbsp;
fine addition to my collection."

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:14.040
Although he's a major player&nbsp;
in the animated Star Wars:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:18.680
The Clone Wars, Grievous' first feature&nbsp;
film appearance also marks his end. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:21.880
he doesn't die at the wrong end&nbsp;
of a Jedi's blade. As a cyborg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:26.760
Grievous has the ability to withstand plenty&nbsp;
of physical damage, even lightsaber strikes.

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:31.600
While hiding out in a cave on a faraway planet,&nbsp;
Grievous is hunted down by Obi-Wan Kenobi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:35.080
who engages with the cyborg and&nbsp;
his droid army. In the battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:39.400
Obi-Wan successfully chops off two of the&nbsp;
general's four cybernetic limbs. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:43.640
he suffers no true injury, the loss of&nbsp;
his hands reduces his effectiveness.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.080
Eventually, Kenobi does kill General Grievous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:49.720
but not with his lightsaber. After&nbsp;
losing his lightsaber in the battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:55.320
Obi-Wan uses a blaster to dispatch the Separatist&nbsp;
leader. Despite his grisly death during the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:59.240
conflict, it's not the lightsaber that&nbsp;
kills him, making General Grievous one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:04.920
of the most durable cyborgs in the galaxy.&nbsp;
Good thing Obi-Wan took him out when he did.

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:09.560
A direct descendant of Darth Vader himself,&nbsp;
Ben Solo fought to walk in the same footsteps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:14.840
as his grandfather. After believing his uncle,&nbsp;
Jedi Master Luke Skywalker, tried to kill him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:19.840
Ben finds refuge with Supreme Leader Snoke,&nbsp;
a clone puppet controlled by the resurrected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:25.280
Palpatine. After changing his name to Kylo Ren,&nbsp;
Ben became the new face of the First Order.

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:29.800
Thirty years after the end of the Empire, the&nbsp;
First Order had left its mark on the galaxy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:32.400
and the New Republic had&nbsp;
all but vanished. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:37.440
a new hero rose up to battle against the Dark&nbsp;
Side: Rey. A young Force-sensitive woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:40.560
who actually turns out to be the&nbsp;
daughter of a clone of Palpatine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:45.520
Rey forms a strange bond with Kylo Ren that turns&nbsp;
slowly into something more. Even after their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:50.640
battle in The Rise of Skywalker ends with Rey&nbsp;
stabbing Ren through the gut, that bond remains.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:55.240
Using a Force-healing technique, Rey keeps&nbsp;
Kylo Ren from death, fighting to resurrect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.240 --> 00:11:00.760
Ben Solo as well. Thankfully, she does, and the&nbsp;
two of them take on Palpatine together. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:06.715
Ben eventually returns the favor to his&nbsp;
friend, giving his life in exchange for Rey's.

00:11:06.715 --> 00:11:10.600
Okay this one is a bit of a stretch,&nbsp;
but Qui-Gon Jinn continues to live on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:15.160
in some form long after plenty of other Jedi&nbsp;
have perished completely, so we thought it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:19.080
would be fair to give him some credit here.&nbsp;
Primarily appearing in The Phantom Menace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:24.400
Qui-Gon trained Obi-Wan since he was a boy, and&nbsp;
planned to train a young Anakin Skywalker as well.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:29.480
Unfortunately, those plans were foiled by the&nbsp;
Sith after the Trade Federation invaded Naboo.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:33.600
As we already know, Darth Maul duels with&nbsp;
Jinn and Kenobi before they're separated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:36.040
and fatally stabs Qui-Gon in the gut.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:41.600
Qui-Gon dies shortly thereafter, but not before&nbsp;
making Obi-Wan swear to train Anakin as a Jedi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:45.880
It's not until the very end of Revenge of the&nbsp;
Sith that Qui-Gon is mentioned again, when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:50.560
Yoda reveals to Obi-Wan that his old master has&nbsp;
found a way to reach out from beyond the grave.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:54.800
At the end of Obi-Wan Kenobi, Qui-Gon&nbsp;
finally reappears to his former apprentice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:59.120
ready to teach him the secret ways of the Force&nbsp;
so that he too might one day join him in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:04.240
afterlife. Admittedly, Qui-Gon doesn't technically&nbsp;
survive his lightsaber wound, but the fact that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:09.534
he learns to make himself into an immortal spirit&nbsp;
following his death definitely gives him an edge.

